      "note": "老松林: the forest path from Snow (npath1-3) winds south and east to the round clearing with the great pine in its middle (clearing); north of it the straight slope (spath1-4, a dead end); east the path to the mossy stone bridge over the gorge, the waterfall pouring into it north of the bridge, and the forest's edge beyond (epath1-3, the broken plank road along the mountain). South the pines close in: pine1-7 and cliffdown are one fixed maze of gaps between the trees (DECISIONS) with a loop, two dead ends and the way on to the cliff's edge in the west; from pine1 one way south to the cliffside, one east to the keep's hidden gate (keep1) and the stockade (keep2: sandbags and stone piles, the stakes; keep3: the bear skin and three chairs, braziers, locked chests, the pit).",
